pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% INTEGRATION-TEST: allow-unchecked-deletion
% Regression: the formula is unsatisfiable (at least two of three variables, but
% pairwise at-most-one). Deleting constraint 2 cannot be proven, so VeriPB falls
% back to unchecked deletion; the `sol` line is then only checked against the
% remaining constraints. A hintless `conclusion SAT` used to be accepted on the
% strength of that solution, because it was validated against
% `best_objective_value` instead of `best_valid_objective_value` (the best value
% logged while checked deletion was still in effect), giving
% `s VERIFIED SATISFIABLE` and exit 0 for an unsatisfiable formula.
f 4 ;
del id 2;
sol x1 x2 ~x3;
output NONE;
conclusion SAT;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
